Modifications made by this project
----------------------------------

Relative to the pinned ROS2 port, this project changes (see
manifests/ros2_fastlivo.patch and manifests/ros2_vikit.patch, and docs/09):

* restored official parameter semantics: `lio.max_iterations` key name,
  `vio.img_point_cov`/`outlier_threshold` as doubles, official defaults for
  `inv_expo_cov`, `patch_pyrimid_level`, `imu_int_frame`, `imu_en`;
* implemented parameter reads that were declared but never used
  (`preprocess.hilti_en`, `pcd_save.type`, `image_save.*`);
* fixed node lifetime/signal handling and the ImageTransport node in main.cpp;
* build fixes: Eigen/PCL 16-byte allocation ABI, x86 `-march=x86-64`, ament
  linking for vikit instead of hard-coded library paths;
* eight YAML configurations restored to the official ROS1 values
  (audited in manifests/config_equivalence.json);
* added the harness: coverage-gated runners, trajectory evaluator, map/video
  rendering, conversion audits, claim audit, cross-platform scripts and docs.

Datasets (not distributed here)
-------------------------------

* Hilti SLAM Challenge 2022 sequences (exp07, exp14, exp18): CC BY-NC-SA 3.0,
  published by Hilti-Research on Hugging Face. Raw bags and derived media that
  we rendered from them are NOT part of this repository; fetch them with
  scripts/download_hf_resumable.py and convert them with scripts/prepare_hilti.py.
  Files under results/ that were derived from these sequences (map previews and
  comparison plots) stay under the same CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 terms: attribution
  required, non-commercial, share-alike.

* Retail_Street: obtained from the public ROS2 mirror referenced by
  DeepRoboticsLab/fast-livo2-deep-robotics. Redistribution terms are unclear,
  therefore this repository ships only the conversion/audit scripts and the
  checksums it computed locally (manifests/data_checksums.json).

